.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwInitAllocator (const \fBGLFWallocator\fP * allocator)"

.PP
Sets the init allocator to the desired value\&. To use the default allocator, call this function with a \fRNULL\fP argument\&.
.PP
If you specify an allocator struct, every member must be a valid function pointer\&. If any member is \fRNULL\fP, this function will emit \fBGLFW_INVALID_VALUE\fP and the init allocator will be unchanged\&.
.PP
The functions in the allocator must fulfil a number of requirements\&. See the documentation for \fBGLFWallocatefun\fP, \fBGLFWreallocatefun\fP and \fBGLFWdeallocatefun\fP for details\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIallocator\fP The allocator to use at the next initialization, or \fRNULL\fP to use the default one\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_INVALID_VALUE\fP\&.
.PP
@pointer_lifetime The specified allocator is copied before this function returns\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
